# The inventory carries public IPs and the admin account name. Neither is a
# secret on its own, but together with this repo's scripts they describe how to
# reach a set of internet-facing lab machines, so the file stays local.
servers.conf

# Collected reports contain account names, login sources, listening ports and
# shell history excerpts. That is exactly the material the review is meant to
# keep internal.
collected/
secreview/
*_report_*.txt
evidence/

# Never commit anything that could hold a credential.
*.pem
*.key
id_*
*secret*
*password*
outputs/
outputs_pack/
*.xlsx

# opencode-linux-x64.tar.gz is vendored on purpose. The release URL in
# setup-opencode.sh is correct, but release assets are served from
# objects.githubusercontent.com, which the lab network blocks even where
# git clone over github.com works. Shipping the binary in the repo is what
# makes "clone and run" true on those hosts. Any OTHER tarball stays out.
*.tar.gz
!opencode-linux-x64.tar.gz
__pycache__/
